    {
      "contentTypeKey": "3ef5c851-77d2-46af-9a22-e2bfadd01829",
      "udi": "umb://element/364b4379138d483fb7c34cb37b7ac1c8",
      "title": "Soil Sampling",
      "content": {
        "markup": "<p>Excellent soil sampling practice is critical to ensure the integrity of testing.</p>\n<p>Failing to take truly representative samples will produce results that do not reflect the true condition of your material.</p>\n<p>Part of excellent practice is collecting soil samples from varying depths and locations. This helps us understand the spatial variation in soil composition and properties across the site. </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>How much soil is enough?</strong></p>\n<p>Typically, 100kg - 120kg of material is a sufficient sample for most soil testing.</p>\n<p>There are factors including sample composition and the scope of testing that may require additional material. You can consult us by sending us a message at the top of the page.</p>",
        "blocks": {
          "contentData": [],
          "settingsData": []
        }
      },
      "images": [
        {
          "key": "1c44785d-ea66-4700-84bc-db3a204cb9a2",
          "mediaKey": "8b1ea1ed-6ae0-45f4-b244-674bb344bdbc"
        }
      ]
    },
